# --- Model provider ---------------------------------------------------------
# Official OpenAI (Responses API). API usage is billed separately from ChatGPT.
# CHAMBER_BACKEND=openai
# CHAMBER_OFFICIAL_OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
# CHAMBER_MODEL=gpt-5.6-luna
# CHAMBER_REASONING_EFFORT=medium
# CHAMBER_OPENAI_API_STYLE=responses

# OpenCode Zen — limited-time free MiMo option (OpenAI-compatible).
# Free-model availability and data handling are controlled by OpenCode Zen.
# This path remains available beside the official OpenAI provider above. The two
# credentials can stay side by side; CHAMBER_BACKEND chooses the active one.
# CHAMBER_BACKEND=opencode
CHAMBER_OPENAI_BASE_URL=https://opencode.ai/zen/v1
OPENCODE_API_KEY=sk-...
CHAMBER_MODEL=mimo-v2.5-free

# Anthropic native
# CHAMBER_ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# CHAMBER_MODEL=claude-sonnet-5

# Force a provider instead of autodetecting: openai | anthropic
# CHAMBER_PROVIDER=openai

# --- Planner (optional) -----------------------------------------------------
# Splits planning from acting. The step model above is called every step and sees
# one stage at a time; the planner is called a handful of times per run — at the
# start, when a stage completes, and when the loop is stuck — and holds the plan
# plus the notes gathered so far.
#
# Why bother: a long task with a cheap model drifts because by step thirty it has
# forgotten there were five laptops. Giving it one stage at a time fixes that, and
# a strong model is affordable when it runs six times instead of fifty.
# Leave unset and the step model plans for itself, exactly as before.
# CHAMBER_ORCHESTRATOR_MODEL=mimo-v2.5-free

# --- Vision (optional) ------------------------------------------------------
# A second, small model that looks at screenshots and answers in words. The
# planner above stays text-only and never sees an image — it reads the
# description. Leave unset to disable; screenshots still save to disk.
#
# Defaults point at Ollama's OpenAI-compatible endpoint, which needs no key:
#   ollama pull qwen2.5vl:3b
# CHAMBER_VISION_MODEL=qwen2.5vl:3b
# CHAMBER_VISION_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1

# Tried only when the local model fails outright or hedges ("I can't see that in
# this part of the screen"). Costs money and latency, so it fires on the cases
# that matter rather than every look.
# CHAMBER_VISION_FALLBACK_MODEL=mimo-v2.5-free

# --- Browser ----------------------------------------------------------------
# Leave unset to autodetect Brave, then ungoogled-chromium, then Chromium.
# CHAMBER_BROWSER=C:\Program Files\BraveSoftware\Brave-Browser\Application\brave.exe

# Live loop display: window (React/Vite Chamber Desk), page (the retained browser
# overlay), or off. The old overlay is kept in the code for compatibility.
CHAMBER_DISPLAY=window

# Where profiles, extensions and run traces live.
# CHAMBER_HOME=C:\Users\you\.chamber
